{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/29335-who-can-grant-exigent-exaltations-who-can-be-granted-one","id":29335,"title":"Who can grant Exigent Exaltations? Who can be granted one?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Exigents"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-13T08:30:46-08:00","id":29335,"title":"Who can grant Exigent Exaltations? Who can be granted one?","content":"We know with a fairly high degree of certainty, that gods can grant an Exigent Exaltation to a mortal, assuming they've been granted the authority / ability by the Sun.<br /> <br /> Could an Elemental? In particular, I'm looking at some of the Heavenly Censors, whom are technically Elementals. (Amusing follow on question; could the Kukla?)<br /> <br /> We know that there are black market Exaltations, Exigence that has escaped into the world of spirits.<br /> Could a demon which acquired such make use of it?<br /> A ghost? A Deathlord?<br /> <br /> Can an Exigent Exaltation be granted to anyone other than a living, mortal human? I can easily imagine a pecular ghost Exalted- not the ghost of an Exalt, but a ghost that is Exalted. What about unelevated animals- Could the Lord of Tyrant Lizards grant their blessing to a single, spectacular Tyrant Lizard, granting it intelligence, long life, nigh invulernability and <a href=\"http://static.comicvine.com/uploads/original/0/1202/103606-108088-devil-dinosaur.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">candy apple red skin</a>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T08:52:56-08:00","id":29344,"title":"","content":"Well, we have been told that demons can't make use of the Exigence, the Unconquered Sun made sure of it. I don't recall anything being said about other types of beings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":868,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","user":"danelsan","date":". 12-13-2013, 11:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T09:13:37-08:00","id":29355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/29335-who-can-grant-exigent-exaltations-who-can-be-granted-one?p=29344#post29344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, we have been told that demons can't make use of the Exigence, the Unconquered Sun made sure of it. I don't recall anything being said about other types of beings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can Exalts create Exigents? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I find the idea of high essence Lawgivers creating Tyke Bombs really interesting. Both as a player and a storyteller.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/239565-wizard-s-panoply-how-to-play-a-mage-in-exalted-collection-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Complete the Wizard's Panoply</a></b> [How to be a mage in Creation]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/442-nephtys","name":"Nephtys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar442_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T09:17:48-08:00","id":29356,"title":"","content":"Who can be granted one: That's pretty easy, it's only creatures with human souls. The same mechanisms work for Exigence soul-pairing as it does for the other Celestial Exaltations. If you can't exalt as a Solar (or Lunar,) you can't Exalt as an Exigent. So no Tyrant Lizard Exalts, sorry.<br /> <br /> Who can grant is much more open. It just seems that you need a certain level of power (no Lesser Gods), access to the Exigence from one way or another, and not be specifically barred from it by the Unconquered Sun, like demons. Other than that, it looks pretty unclear, probably on purpose so it can vary from ST to ST.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/845-dragonmystic","name":"Dragonmystic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar845_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T09:29:07-08:00","id":29359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/29335-who-can-grant-exigent-exaltations-who-can-be-granted-one?p=29344#post29344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, we have been told that demons can't make use of the Exigence, the Unconquered Sun made sure of it. I don't recall anything being said about other types of beings.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's definitely one thing I'll be changing for my games. There are too many 2nd and 3rd circle demons that I would love to create Exigents for.d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T09:37:54-08:00","id":29365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/29335-who-can-grant-exigent-exaltations-who-can-be-granted-one?p=29359#post29359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's definitely one thing I'll be changing for my games. There are too many 2nd and 3rd circle demons that I would love to create Exigents for.d</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Completely agree. Limiting exigents to gods cuts out a huge swath of possibilities. Though I suppose I understand why from a story perspective. Maybe black market exaltations will provide some sort of work around?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1092-tribute-of-a-dark-heart","name":"Tribute of a Dark Heart","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1092_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T09:39:41-08:00","id":29366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/29335-who-can-grant-exigent-exaltations-who-can-be-granted-one#post29335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about unelevated animals?</div> </div> </div> </div>My personal hope is that the Animal Avatars are reclassified as the once every generation paragons of the species they belong to rather than a vaguely defined type of god.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T09:44:34-08:00","id":29368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tribute of a Dark Heart</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/29335-who-can-grant-exigent-exaltations-who-can-be-granted-one?p=29365#post29365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Limiting exigents to gods cuts out a huge swath of possibilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or you can just give everyone else their own thing instead of forcing the Exigence to do something it isn't mechanically or narratively designed to do.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T10:03:50-08:00","id":29374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/29335-who-can-grant-exigent-exaltations-who-can-be-granted-one?p=29359#post29359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's definitely one thing I'll be changing for my games. There are too many 2nd and 3rd circle demons that I would love to create Exigents for.d</div> </div> </div> </div>Go for it. Exigence is tailor-made to be house-ruled, after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/845-dragonmystic","name":"Dragonmystic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar845_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T10:17:05-08:00","id":29378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/29335-who-can-grant-exigent-exaltations-who-can-be-granted-one?p=29344#post29344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, we have been told that demons can't make use of the Exigence, the Unconquered Sun made sure of it. I don't recall anything being said about other types of beings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? I thought it was implied they could via Black Market ones? Or at least corrupt ones they got a hold of somehow?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/448-dulahan","name":"Dulahan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T10:34:45-08:00","id":29391,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Exigence has a lot of promise, but within the setting it seems to be primarily a thing to assist sufficiently worthy and desperate gods.<br /> <br /> We've got Liminals, Getimians and Exalts yet unrevealed (including probably some Infernals) to demonstrate that there can be new Exalts that aren't Exigents (even if the book for Exigents is also the place where we're given the guidelines to devise new Exalted).<br /> <br /> What the Exigence specifically being unable to be used by demons takes away is something they probably think the setting shouldn't have.<br /> <br /> You might as well say limiting Wyld-Shaping Technique to Solars cuts out a huge swath of possibilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T10:37:50-08:00","id":29393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dragonmystic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/29335-who-can-grant-exigent-exaltations-who-can-be-granted-one?p=29356#post29356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The same mechanisms work for Exigence soul-pairing as it does for the other Celestial Exaltations.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems unlikely, considering that they've stated that there can be Exigents who work comparably to Terrestrials, Alchemicals, and stranger things besides.<br /> <br /> Like, humans yeah, but distinguishing by souls, is... odd. Nothing that isn't human has a human soul, and nothing that is human doesn't have a soul (barring some really transgressive magic).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T10:58:43-08:00","id":29409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/29335-who-can-grant-exigent-exaltations-who-can-be-granted-one?p=29391#post29391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What the Exigence specifically being unable to be used by demons takes away is something they probably think the setting shouldn't have.</div> </div> </div> </div>A 3rd Circle Soul creating his own Exalt to further his own themes, instead of Infernals furthering Hell's and/or a major theme/concept of a complete Yozi?<br /> I like the idea quite much to design Malfeas similar to Yu-Shan, with political power play, cheating and gambling for power. Bringing in the need of demon to have his own Exigent, similar to a god in Yu-Shan who has no other option than to bring in an Exalt on his side.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/239565-wizard-s-panoply-how-to-play-a-mage-in-exalted-collection-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Complete the Wizard's Panoply</a></b> [How to be a mage in Creation]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/442-nephtys","name":"Nephtys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar442_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T11:04:03-08:00","id":29411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nephtys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/29335-who-can-grant-exigent-exaltations-who-can-be-granted-one?p=29409#post29409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A 3rd Circle Soul creating his own Exalt to further his own themes, instead of Infernals furthering Hell's and/or a major theme/concept of a complete Yozi?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We've got Liminals, Getimians and Exalts yet unrevealed (including probably some Infernals) to demonstrate that there can be new Exalts that aren't Exigents </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nephtys</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea quite much to design Malfeas similar to Yu-Shan, with political power play, cheating and gambling for power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hell already has its own forms of politics, I see nothing of value by homogenizing them with Heaven.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nephtys</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bringing in the need of demon to have his own Exigent, similar to a god in Yu-Shan who has no other option than to bring in an Exalt on his side.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really hope that that's not going to be an implication of Exigence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T11:44:31-08:00","id":29435,"title":"","content":"Just because demons don't use Exigence doesn't mean there can't be new Demon Chosen!<br /> It just means they weren't made via the Sun's blessings. Why would demons want that anyway?<br /> <br /> If you want them to exist, say they exist! The Exigence is an in-setting excuse to add new varieties of exalts, but it is by no means the only way they can exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/103-gsd","name":"GSD","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T15:00:24-08:00","id":29547,"title":"","content":"Seriously. The devs have been incredibly clear about how EX3 is meant to be very, very friendly to custom Exalts. Is it that tons of people missed that, tons of people misunderstood or ignored that, or <i>I'm</i> completely misunderstanding them? I am hopeful the EX3 team plans to put this explicitly into print, to make clear that it's 100% okay and supported for people to do so.<br /> <br /> Exigents absolutely do not constitute the box into which you cram every single custom Exalt that isn't canonically described. They constitute a specific box -- albeit an unusually broad one -- that is meant to inspire the custom creation of further boxes. The tools in the Exigent book will be as valuable for Exigents as they will for existing splats as they will for any non-Exigent custom Exalts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T15:29:45-08:00","id":29574,"title":"","content":"The Exigence is for gods only. That said, you paid for the book, tell the story you want to tell.<br /> <br /> The point of the Exigents wasn't to create a new box all new Exalts had to fit in, though, but rather to communicate that you can add whatever you like to the game (and to remove most of the mental heavy lifting from the most obvious avenue people would want to pursue).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":20}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/84-holden","name":"Holden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar84_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"673"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T17:52:01-08:00","id":29641,"title":"","content":"Well...I imagine Demons DON'T use it, rather than explicitly can't... because the Yozi tried making their own Exalted, and it disquieted them. I imagine they ban their souls from using it to prevent any sort of rabid degeneration of their own power or minds, as the Exigence definitely has negative effects on the one who utilizes it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/697-arteliex","name":"Arteliex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar697_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T23:03:28-08:00","id":29763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arteliex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/29335-who-can-grant-exigent-exaltations-who-can-be-granted-one?p=29641#post29641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well...I imagine Demons DON'T use it, rather than explicitly can't... because the Yozi tried making their own Exalted, and it disquieted them. I imagine they ban their souls from using it to prevent any sort of rabid degeneration of their own power or minds, as the Exigence definitely has negative effects on the one who utilizes it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not that the Exigence has negative effects - it does - it's that the process of creating Exalted, period, appears to negatively impact the creator. Unless I've missed something, the Exigence is not the origin of Exaltation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T23:09:53-08:00","id":29765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/29335-who-can-grant-exigent-exaltations-who-can-be-granted-one?p=29574#post29574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Exigence is for gods only. That said, you paid for the book, tell the story you want to tell.<br /> <br /> <u><b>The point of the Exigents wasn't to create a new box all new Exalts had to fit in, though</b></u>, but rather to communicate that you can add whatever you like to the game (and to remove most of the mental heavy lifting from the most obvious avenue people would want to pursue).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I'm a bit worried that, because Exigents were announced as a thing now, that people's creative efforts would focus all Exalt creation into Exigents <i>as a category</i>... Want to make up a new Exalt type? Nah, just make an Exigent. Have a cool idea that doesn't fall in the Terrestrial/Celestial category? Exigent. Exigent? Exigent.<br /> <br /> (Well, not that you exactly need to make tons of new Exalted per se... Fan creations have always been a thing.)<br /> <br /> The fact that Getimians will be here, and that Liminal Exalted will be introduced -- <i>and </i>Liminals are apparently new(ish) to Creation... That last part, I feel, probably sends the strongest message. By having a new Exalted come into being <i>after </i>the Primordial War.<br /> <br /> Hell, apparently there were even stranger Exalted around -- I think I vaguely recall some mention of the Niobraran having Exalts of their own?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/266-ochre","name":"Ochre","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-07T14:25:57-08:00","id":67413,"title":"","content":"what are Niobraran?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://jaxushomebrew.blogspot.ie/2016/06/introduction-site-map-and-catalogue.html\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew blog</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1291-mr-jaxus","name":"Mr.Jaxus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-07T14:44:16-08:00","id":67429,"title":"","content":"The Niobraran League is a collective of aquatic races who predate humanity, who rallied together in fear against the Exalted upon realizing they had taken down the Lintha during the War. <br /> <br /> They have their own champions--I think they were called &quot;Spoken&quot;, but I have no idea where I'm pulling that from--and very nearly won. Their story, in the (hopefully upcoming?) Heroes of the Niobraran supplement, is there to show that the Exalted--even all together--are not some invincible juggernaut that gets to LOLstomp everything, nor LOLstomp the consequences of their LOLstompage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-07T17:30:20-08:00","id":67506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/29335-who-can-grant-exigent-exaltations-who-can-be-granted-one#post29335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about unelevated animals- Could the Lord of Tyrant Lizards grant their blessing to a single, spectacular Tyrant Lizard, granting it intelligence, long life, nigh invulernability and <a href=\"http://static.comicvine.com/uploads/original/0/1202/103606-108088-devil-dinosaur.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">candy apple red skin</a>?</div> </div> </div> </div>Or perhaps a tie, a goatee, and about <a href=\"http://drmcninja.com/archives/comic/21p97/\" target=\"_blank\">a million dots in Charisma</a>?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-07T21:11:25-08:00","id":67687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/29335-who-can-grant-exigent-exaltations-who-can-be-granted-one?p=67429#post67429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Niobraran League is a collective of aquatic races who predate humanity, who rallied together in fear against the Exalted upon realizing they had taken down the Lintha during the War.<br /> <br /> They have their own champions--I think they were called &quot;Spoken&quot;, but I have no idea where I'm pulling that from--and very nearly won. Their story, in the (hopefully upcoming?) Heroes of the Niobraran supplement, is there to show that the Exalted--even all together--are not some invincible juggernaut that gets to LOLstomp everything, nor LOLstomp the consequences of their LOLstompage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, <i>two</i> varieties of Exalt have been mentioned as being on their side, the Spoken, and the Chosen of Depths! It sounds like the book itself is conceived as one part alternate era scenario you could run a game set in, and one part cool remnants and ruins full of exciting creatures and possibilities for Exalted games in the standard Realm Year 768.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/91-wandering","name":"Wandering","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar91_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-07T21:24:10-08:00","id":67697,"title":"","content":"You know, one thing I find interesting are the &quot;Black Market&quot; exaltations. I feel like those might end up bartered by unscrupulous gods to entities like 3rd circle demons or forbidden gods, though if its intended as a specific thing for gods only, I kinda get that. Still, that whole exchange could make for an interesting Sidereal story...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1334-magistercrow","name":"MagisterCrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1334_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-07T21:43:12-08:00","id":67710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nephtys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/29335-who-can-grant-exigent-exaltations-who-can-be-granted-one?p=29355#post29355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Exalts create Exigents? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I find the idea of high essence Lawgivers creating Tyke Bombs really interesting. Both as a player and a storyteller.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this would be a great idea and I'm using it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-09T21:33:33-08:00","id":68807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nephtys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/29335-who-can-grant-exigent-exaltations-who-can-be-granted-one?p=29355#post29355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Exalts create Exigents?</div> </div> </div> </div>I kind of hope they don't, to be honest.<br /> <br /> Although it's the goal of the new edition to make Exalts more widely varied in all their forms, I'd like to see Exaltation remain special and catacylsmic in it's own right. It kills at least some of those who attempt it. The Yozis decided that their own army of super-soldier just wasn't worth the consequences ... and they managed to stick to that as a group. It's possibly the single thing they've all agreed on for the longest. I guess I'd like to see that they Gods who could, politically, mostly don't because their existance is pretty good, really, and they don't want to go through the metaphysical lung-and-kidney transplant that seems to be required. As for the Gods (or other beings) that do use it ... they have to. They don't see they have any other choice. They don't want Exalts, they <i>need</i> them.<br /> <br /> Black market Exaltations are talked about more in the hushed and uncertain terms black market nukes are, that the sort of legal and financial hubbub about black market heroin.<br /> <br /> Which is not to say that I'm not sympathetic to the making of TykeBombs, just that I don't think this is a good way to do it. Ochre's point is a good one, Creation is better off filled with half-breeds, Imbued Amalgams, Genesis-products, Tiger-Warriors (and subjects of other, similar Charms), olichike, and Wyld-forged prodigies than having everyone who wants to empower a mortal think 'well, it's off to the Excigence again'.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1849-suddenthunder","name":"SuddenThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-09T21:55:20-08:00","id":68829,"title":"","content":"It's hard to make a new Exalt that isn't crappy. I know because I drew plans for many that never will see the light of day.<br /> <br /> I designed the Exigence to make it easy on people to come up with their own Exalts and shuck the origin, and toss it out the window. &quot;It's an Exigent,&quot; case closed. It might be based on a god you know, or it might be a dirty bomb or black market job, something that has powers and metaphysical traits you wouldn't expect. <br /> <br /> See also: the Guild Barber. What is he Chosen of? What indeed. (Hint: It's not the god of haircuts.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-09T22:25:00-08:00","id":68843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/29335-who-can-grant-exigent-exaltations-who-can-be-granted-one?p=67429#post67429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Niobraran League is a collective of aquatic races who predate humanity, who rallied together in fear against the Exalted upon realizing they had taken down the Lintha during the War.<br /> <br /> They have their own champions--I think they were called &quot;Spoken&quot;, but I have no idea where I'm pulling that from--and very nearly won. Their story, in the (hopefully upcoming?) Heroes of the Niobraran supplement, is there to show that the Exalted--even all together--are not some invincible juggernaut that gets to LOLstomp everything, nor LOLstomp the consequences of their LOLstompage.</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't all necessarily predate humanity. The Niobraran League was a group of aquatic races including human mutants and also nonhumans (some of whom predated humanity and some of whom didn't, one assumes), who collectively formed a power bloc in the Undersea, and who went to war with the Exalted for mastery of Creation following the Primordials' defeat. The Exalted won but it was a close thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-09T22:42:57-08:00","id":68854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/29335-who-can-grant-exigent-exaltations-who-can-be-granted-one?p=68829#post68829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's hard to make a new Exalt that isn't crappy. I know because I drew plans for many that never will see the light of day.<br /> <br /> I designed the Exigence to make it easy on people to come up with their own Exalts and shuck the origin, and toss it out the window. &quot;It's an Exigent,&quot; case closed. It might be based on a god you know, or it might be a dirty bomb or black market job, something that has powers and metaphysical traits you wouldn't expect.<br /> <br /> See also: the Guild Barber. What is he Chosen of? What indeed. (Hint: It's not the god of haircuts.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel that, properly executed, the God of Haircuts would be an unimaginably terrifying foe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-10T01:46:01-08:00","id":68901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuddenThunder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/29335-who-can-grant-exigent-exaltations-who-can-be-granted-one?p=68807#post68807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I kind of hope they don't, to be honest.<br /> <br /> Although it's the goal of the new edition to make Exalts more widely varied in all their forms, I'd like to see Exaltation remain special and catacylsmic in it's own right. It kills at least some of those who attempt it. The Yozis decided that their own army of super-soldier just wasn't worth the consequences ... and they managed to stick to that as a group. It's possibly the single thing they've all agreed on for the longest. I guess I'd like to see that they Gods who could, politically, mostly don't because their existance is pretty good, really, and they don't want to go through the metaphysical lung-and-kidney transplant that seems to be required. As for the Gods (or other beings) that do use it ... they have to. They don't see they have any other choice. They don't want Exalts, they <i>need</i> them.<br /> <br /> Black market Exaltations are talked about more in the hushed and uncertain terms black market nukes are, that the sort of legal and financial hubbub about black market heroin.<br /> <br /> Which is not to say that I'm not sympathetic to the making of TykeBombs, just that I don't think this is a good way to do it. Ochre's point is a good one, Creation is better off filled with half-breeds, Imbued Amalgams, Genesis-products, Tiger-Warriors (and subjects of other, similar Charms), olichike, and Wyld-forged prodigies than having everyone who wants to empower a mortal think 'well, it's off to the Excigence again'.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that exalted created exalts isn't something that can't work-- so long as it doesn't ever get to &quot;production line.&quot; My take on it, that I'm going to use for any game where this comes up, is that every exalt is, thematically and even mechanically, not a part of hte setting, it's something that to a greater or lesser degree *drives* the setting-- and a big prt of the setting is &quot;foromer underlings sometimes exceed their creators vision or just outright gank him.&quot; Whenever you create an exalt you create a hero (or villain) who cannot be controlled. So sure-- go on a glorious quest (because there is no instruction manual) to claim the fire of heaven for your follower orboon companion-- but it will always be different, it will always be unusual, it will always be earthsaking...and sometimes, when you grab for heaven's fire, you get burned.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-10T01:47:19-08:00","id":68902,"title":"","content":"Another question-- Autocthon could grant a style of exigent exaltation, couldn't he, since he sort of invented exaltation. They couldn't, obviously be empowered by the Sun, but I could see the divine ministers possibly having the authority to make use of some of his sleeping power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-10T04:59:58-08:00","id":68970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NewK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/29335-who-can-grant-exigent-exaltations-who-can-be-granted-one?p=68902#post68902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another question-- Autocthon could grant a style of exigent exaltation, couldn't he, since he sort of invented exaltation. They couldn't, obviously be empowered by the Sun, but I could see the divine ministers possibly having the authority to make use of some of his sleeping power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that depends a bit on what exactly the Exigence is, something very little has been said about. <br /> <br /> He could almost certainly teach another God or Primordial to make Exalts. He's done it before. Whether that would be a different thing to using the Exigence to create one is an open question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1849-suddenthunder","name":"SuddenThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-10T05:06:39-08:00","id":68972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NewK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/29335-who-can-grant-exigent-exaltations-who-can-be-granted-one?p=68901#post68901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So sure-- go on a glorious quest (because there is no instruction manual) to claim the fire of heaven for your follower orboon companion-- but it will always be different, it will always be unusual, it will always be earthsaking...and sometimes, when you grab for heaven's fire, you get burned.</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely a solid foundation for a story. I just don't think the Exigence makes it better.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1849-suddenthunder","name":"SuddenThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-10T05:55:08-08:00","id":69005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NewK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/29335-who-can-grant-exigent-exaltations-who-can-be-granted-one?p=68902#post68902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another question-- Autocthon could grant a style of exigent exaltation, couldn't he, since he sort of invented exaltation. They couldn't, obviously be empowered by the Sun, but I could see the divine ministers possibly having the authority to make use of some of his sleeping power.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think beings who can already make their own Exalted can't use Exigence.<br /> <br /> Exigence, by definition, seems to be a leg up for beings who lack the means to bring forth their own Exalted.<br /> <br /> That sounds like something that could be granted to the Divine Ministers, but I don't think Autochthon could do it; I think something in the quality of Exigence is a bit particular to the Unconquered Sun.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-10T06:50:25-08:00","id":69032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/29335-who-can-grant-exigent-exaltations-who-can-be-granted-one?p=29574#post29574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Exigence is for gods only. That said, you paid for the book, tell the story you want to tell.<br /> <br /> The point of the Exigents wasn't to create a new box all new Exalts had to fit in, though, but rather to communicate that you can add whatever you like to the game (and to remove most of the mental heavy lifting from the most obvious avenue people would want to pursue).</div> </div> </div> </div>This leads me to a question. What happens if the Unconquered Sun creates an Exigent of his own. Would it, essentially, simply be another Solar Exalted? And if Luna made an Exigent, would you end up with a Lunar? Or would you end up with something different?<br /> <br /> Exigents basically take the concepts and themes of their patron and run with that. So, if someone really liked say, Ligier and decided to make an Exalt based around him, it probably wouldn't be much different, at its core, from Exigents who draws heavily from from a single patron's themes.<br /> <br /> There are plenty of Exalted who don't work that way (such as Gentimians, Liminals and Alchemicals) and Exalts who draw from multiple patrons/themes (Sidereal and Dragon Blooded). So there's plenty of room for Exalted who aren't Exigents. <br /> <br /> But, from what little we know about them, it seems that if you wanted to make an Exalt designed to be empowered by a single patron (say an ancient ghost or a powerful demon) then Exigents would be a very good place to start.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-10T06:59:50-08:00","id":69041,"title":"","content":"There was definitely something where John said the Incarnae cannot use the Exigence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-10T07:14:02-08:00","id":69048,"title":"","content":"Incarnae can't use the Exigence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-10T07:24:28-08:00","id":69055,"title":"","content":"That works for me, thanks, John!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-10T07:33:50-08:00","id":69065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Creation is better off filled with half-breeds, Imbued Amalgams, Genesis-products, Tiger-Warriors (and subjects of other, similar Charms), olichike, and Wyld-forged prodigies than having everyone who wants to empower a mortal think 'well, it's off to the Excigence again'. </div> </div> </div>Had a PC whose Followers ended up being magically-loyal Science of Mutation-enhanced Tiger Warrior Legendary Scholar Terrestrial Sorcerer Terrestrial Martial Artist gods-blessed Artifact-wielding Artifact-armored immortals with thaumaturgy. Took a long time to get 'em that way. I was proud of 'em.<br /> <br /> Then the ST started making &quot;Space Marine&quot; jokes, constantly, and made a point of dicelessly killing one off during a dramatic moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-10T07:52:35-08:00","id":69074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/29335-who-can-grant-exigent-exaltations-who-can-be-granted-one?p=69041#post69041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was definitely something where John said the Incarnae cannot use the Exigence.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/29335-who-can-grant-exigent-exaltations-who-can-be-granted-one?p=69048#post69048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incarnae can't use the Exigence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Note to self: Isator Levi can <i>see the future</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-10T09:30:52-08:00","id":69135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/29335-who-can-grant-exigent-exaltations-who-can-be-granted-one?p=69074#post69074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Note to self: Isator Levi can <i>see the future</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, he does have approximate knowledge of many things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1794-doran","name":"doran","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1794_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-10T12:32:35-08:00","id":69298,"title":"","content":"Makes sense. The Incarnae already have their own Exalted, they don't need to make more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-10T13:26:03-08:00","id":69343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dragonmystic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/29335-who-can-grant-exigent-exaltations-who-can-be-granted-one?p=29356#post29356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who can be granted one: That's pretty easy, it's only creatures with human souls. The same mechanisms work for Exigence soul-pairing as it does for the other Celestial Exaltations. If you can't exalt as a Solar (or Lunar,) you can't Exalt as an Exigent. So no Tyrant Lizard Exalts, sorry.</div> </div> </div> </div>It really depends on why you want a Tyrant Lizard Exalt. If you just want the aesthetics, I'm certain that the Chosen of Tyrant Lizards will get the ability to turn into a Tyrant Lizard. Not much point in being Chosen otherwise, is there?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1369-mewtarthio","name":"Mewtarthio","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-10T13:52:23-08:00","id":69392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mewtarthio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/29335-who-can-grant-exigent-exaltations-who-can-be-granted-one?p=69343#post69343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It really depends on why you want a Tyrant Lizard Exalt. If you just want the aesthetics, I'm certain that the Chosen of Tyrant Lizards will get the ability to turn into a Tyrant Lizard. Not much point in being Chosen otherwise, is there?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would design animal-totemed Exigents around familiars, rather than shapeshifting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-10T14:21:06-08:00","id":69417,"title":"","content":"Um, not to be too much of a pill, but isn't there an existing Exalt type which has some ability to maybe turn into a Tyrant Lizard in some manner?<br /> <br /> Pedantry aside, the only animal <i>god</i> in Creation I can think of off hand (not an Animal Avatar, since those are a whole other, albeit poorly-defined, thing) is Ahlat, who (based on his actions as the God of War And Cattle) seems to have interpreted &quot;God of Cattle&quot; as governing human cultivation of cattle, rather than representing the interests of the cattle themselves. That seems to support Robert Vance's idea of Familiar-like effects, but even that isn't something Ahlat is known for. He doesn't seem to deal directly with cattle much at all, save insofar as some Super Cattle Spirits work for him. His actual abilities are more based around emulating cattle, in terms of making people act as herds driven by angry leaders, promoting fertility, etc. From that point of view, a Chosen of (The God of) Tyrant Lizards might just have Charms for scaring people and hitting really hard, and amazing tracking.<br /> <br /> ... though all of those also sound like specialties of some other sort of Exalt, which could also be closely tied to Tyrant Lizards. Hurm. Why are we going out of our way to concept this as an Exigent, again?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-10T14:26:51-08:00","id":69424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/29335-who-can-grant-exigent-exaltations-who-can-be-granted-one?p=69417#post69417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... though all of those also sound like specialties of some other sort of Exalt, which could also be closely tied to Tyrant Lizards. Hurm. Why are we going out of our way to concept this as an Exigent, again?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Hero with a magical dog&quot; is too rich and resonant a thing to not eventually show up somehow as an Exigent design. It is plausible that an Exigent that fulfilled that role might also be designed to be compatible with other choices of magical companion species. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-10T14:41:14-08:00","id":69433,"title":"","content":"&quot;Hero with a magical dog&quot; is something that Solars and Sidereals both could do pretty well in 2E, and anyone else could take a crack at using Familiar.<br /> <br /> If Exigents open up a new way to approach it, that's fine, and can be really neat - the strength Exigents, narratively, seems to be the range of elements they can interface with. But I do not feel any anxiet over whether there will be three Charm trees which are strong fits for this concept, or merely two.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-10T16:21:49-08:00","id":69485,"title":"","content":"&quot;Hero and magical dog&quot; Exigent, go! First Familiar Charm: <a href=\"http://adventuretime.wikia.com/wiki/Jakesuit\" target=\"_blank\">Jake-suit</a> Combination Prana, Activate!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 02-10-2014, 07:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-10T16:58:59-08:00","id":69502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/29335-who-can-grant-exigent-exaltations-who-can-be-granted-one?p=68829#post68829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See also: the Guild Barber. What is he Chosen of? What indeed. (Hint: It's not the god of haircuts.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I cannot be the only one who thinks his divine patron is/was a (group of?) Bloody Hand(s)?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-10T17:01:50-08:00","id":69505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mewtarthio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/29335-who-can-grant-exigent-exaltations-who-can-be-granted-one?p=69343#post69343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It really depends on why you want a Tyrant Lizard Exalt. If you just want the aesthetics, I'm certain that the Chosen of Tyrant Lizards will get the ability to turn into a Tyrant Lizard. Not much point in being Chosen otherwise, is there?</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the Exigent ideas I came up that I'm likely to actually homebrew eventually was an Attribute-based Chosen of Cats, and my thought process went something like this: &quot;Hmm, that's an idea. But it would be kind of redundant with a cat-themed Lunar, wouldn't it? Oh, but trying to make it still feel appropriate while <i>also </i>being very different from that would be an interesting challenge!&quot; And so my two immediate resolutions were: don't write it until after Lunars is out, and don't give them any shapeshifting whatsoever, not even retractable claws or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-10T20:09:45-08:00","id":69580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/29335-who-can-grant-exigent-exaltations-who-can-be-granted-one?p=68854#post68854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel that, properly executed, the God of Haircuts would be an unimaginably terrifying foe.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"http://www.furinkan.com/ranma/characters/principalmanga.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> I'm inclined to concur with your reasoning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-10T21:07:49-08:00","id":69603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/29335-who-can-grant-exigent-exaltations-who-can-be-granted-one?p=69424#post69424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Hero with a magical dog&quot; is too rich and resonant a thing to not eventually show up somehow as an Exigent design. It is plausible that an Exigent that fulfilled that role might also be designed to be compatible with other choices of magical companion species.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can think of <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Puss_in_Boots\" target=\"_blank\">one noteworthy example</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-10T21:16:17-08:00","id":69609,"title":"","content":"Funny, I always viewed Puss as a schemer Sidereal or a trickster Lunar. I'd definitely love to see an exigent that draws on one of my favorite fairy tales, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T01:27:23-08:00","id":69690,"title":"","content":"Of course, we should note that making an exalted using the rules in the exigent rulebook and making an <i>Exigent</i> exalt, as in one that is the product of a god's petition to the Unconquered Sun are two different things...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-17T00:03:43-08:00","id":73589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/29335-who-can-grant-exigent-exaltations-who-can-be-granted-one?p=69065#post69065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Had a PC whose Followers ended up being magically-loyal Science of Mutation-enhanced Tiger Warrior Legendary Scholar Terrestrial Sorcerer Terrestrial Martial Artist gods-blessed Artifact-wielding Artifact-armored immortals with thaumaturgy. Took a long time to get 'em that way. I was proud of 'em.<br /> <br /> Then the ST started making &quot;Space Marine&quot; jokes, constantly, and made a point of dicelessly killing one off during a dramatic moment.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Sigh&quot;...what a Jerk. Sorry...but that was a jerkish thing to do.<br /> <br /> ~ N","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is timing in everything. Timing in strategy cannot be mastered without a great deal of practice. There is also timing in the Void. You win battles with the timing in the Void born of the timing of cunning by knowing the enemies' timing, and thus using a timing which the enemy does not expect.&quot; <i>Shinmen Musashi no Kami Fujiwara no Genshin, Go Rin No Sho (The Book of the Five Rings)</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2141-nadrakas","name":"Nadrakas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2141_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-17T00:05:46-08:00","id":73592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/29335-who-can-grant-exigent-exaltations-who-can-be-granted-one?p=69502#post69502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I cannot be the only one who thinks his divine patron is/was a (group of?) Bloody Hand(s)?</div> </div> </div> </div>LoL.......nope, you are not the only one.<br /> <br /> ~ N","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is timing in everything. Timing in strategy cannot be mastered without a great deal of practice. There is also timing in the Void. You win battles with the timing in the Void born of the timing of cunning by knowing the enemies' timing, and thus using a timing which the enemy does not expect.&quot; <i>Shinmen Musashi no Kami Fujiwara no Genshin, Go Rin No Sho (The Book of the Five Rings)</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2141-nadrakas","name":"Nadrakas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2141_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-17T00:06:58-08:00","id":73593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/29335-who-can-grant-exigent-exaltations-who-can-be-granted-one?p=69505#post69505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One of the Exigent ideas I came up that I'm likely to actually homebrew eventually was an Attribute-based Chosen of Cats, and my thought process went something like this: &quot;Hmm, that's an idea. But it would be kind of redundant with a cat-themed Lunar, wouldn't it? Oh, but trying to make it still feel appropriate while <i>also </i>being very different from that would be an interesting challenge!&quot; And so my two immediate resolutions were: don't write it until after Lunars is out, and don't give them any shapeshifting whatsoever, not even retractable claws or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well...remind me to never play my Chosen of Mice around you're Chosen of Cats.<br /> <br /> ~ N","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is timing in everything. Timing in strategy cannot be mastered without a great deal of practice. There is also timing in the Void. You win battles with the timing in the Void born of the timing of cunning by knowing the enemies' timing, and thus using a timing which the enemy does not expect.&quot; <i>Shinmen Musashi no Kami Fujiwara no Genshin, Go Rin No Sho (The Book of the Five Rings)</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2141-nadrakas","name":"Nadrakas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2141_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-17T02:14:47-08:00","id":73632,"title":"","content":"Honestly, one thing I hope is that the 3E lunars are sufficiently broad in concept that it's possible to have other exalts that also can shape change without feeling like we're walking over the Lunars territory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-17T05:14:03-08:00","id":73664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nadrakas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/29335-who-can-grant-exigent-exaltations-who-can-be-granted-one?p=73589#post73589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> &quot;Sigh&quot;...what a Jerk. Sorry...but that was a jerkish thing to do. ~ N</div> </div> </div> </div>I've got a depressingly-large number of examples of this kind of stuff, largely because all of us players wanted to keep playing our characters, and the ST was the only one willing to run it for us.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-17T07:38:42-08:00","id":73711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/29335-who-can-grant-exigent-exaltations-who-can-be-granted-one?p=73664#post73664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've got a depressingly-large number of examples of this kind of stuff, largely because all of us players wanted to keep playing our characters, and the ST was the only one willing to run it for us.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Sigh&quot;...yeah. I really do understand -- I've had to rescue more than a few games (Not bragging...maybe we'll all sit down some day and talk somewhere -- online or in-real-life...). For another thread...another day. ;( For now, let's move on to happier things -- let's move on to more Exigent's. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> ~ N","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is timing in everything. Timing in strategy cannot be mastered without a great deal of practice. There is also timing in the Void. You win battles with the timing in the Void born of the timing of cunning by knowing the enemies' timing, and thus using a timing which the enemy does not expect.&quot; <i>Shinmen Musashi no Kami Fujiwara no Genshin, Go Rin No Sho (The Book of the Five Rings)</i>","edited":{"userid":2141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2141-nadrakas","user":"Nadrakas","date":". 02-17-2014, 10:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2141-nadrakas","name":"Nadrakas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2141_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T04:48:25-07:00","id":164709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/29335-who-can-grant-exigent-exaltations-who-can-be-granted-one?p=29359#post29359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's definitely one thing I'll be changing for my games. There are too many 2nd and 3rd circle demons that I would love to create Exigents for.d</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering 2nd and 3rd circle demons can already make <b>akuma</b>, seems pretty unnecessary to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/29335-who-can-grant-exigent-exaltations-who-can-be-granted-one?p=29366#post29366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My personal hope is that the Animal Avatars are reclassified as the once every generation paragons of the species they belong to rather than a vaguely defined type of god.</div> </div> </div> </div>What if they were reclassified to a vaguely defined type of <b>non-human exalt</b>, as was at least partly implied by their original fluff?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 06-10-2014, 07:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T05:01:43-07:00","id":164732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/29335-who-can-grant-exigent-exaltations-who-can-be-granted-one?p=164709#post164709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Considering 2nd and 3rd circle demons can already make <b>akuma</b>, seems pretty unnecessary to me.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure Akuma can't create their own charm which is the fun part of Exigents. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T05:03:39-07:00","id":164734,"title":"","content":"I would find the personal Exalts of individual demons far more interesting than Akuma as they currently stand. Perhaps that will change, but I doubt it.<br /> <br /> For that matter I would find the Exalted of demons far more interesting than Green Sun Princes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T05:04:32-07:00","id":164735,"title":"","content":"I thought Akuma were getting the chop in 3E anyway?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T05:18:11-07:00","id":164739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/29335-who-can-grant-exigent-exaltations-who-can-be-granted-one?p=164735#post164735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought Akuma were getting the chop in 3E anyway?</div> </div> </div> </div>I seem to recall that they are being changed drastically, but the concept of dark pacts with elder powers will remain. I'll need to check up on that later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T16:27:27-07:00","id":165347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wandering</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/29335-who-can-grant-exigent-exaltations-who-can-be-granted-one?p=67687#post67687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, <i>two</i> varieties of Exalt have been mentioned as being on their side, the Spoken, and the Chosen of Depths! It sounds like the book itself is conceived as one part alternate era scenario you could run a game set in, and one part cool remnants and ruins full of exciting creatures and possibilities for Exalted games in the standard Realm Year 768.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this Niobraran League a book that is confirmed to be coming out sometime in the near future?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1522,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","user":"turkeygiant","date":". 06-10-2014, 07:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T17:01:15-07:00","id":165377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/29335-who-can-grant-exigent-exaltations-who-can-be-granted-one?p=165347#post165347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is this Niobraran League a book that is confirmed to be coming out sometime in the near future?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would wager that John knows exactly where he wants it on the schedule, but it's not in the first 12-18 months of books, which means that we don't have a date and he has to convince OPP to let him write it. It sounds like they're pretty serious about making it happen, though, and I definitely got the impression that they were hoping to have it out before the weird hardbacks like Infernals and Alchemicals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T17:05:25-07:00","id":165388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/29335-who-can-grant-exigent-exaltations-who-can-be-granted-one?p=165377#post165377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would wager that John knows exactly where he wants it on the schedule, but it's not in the first 12-18 months of books, which means that we don't have a date and he has to convince OPP to let him write it. It sounds like they're pretty serious about making it happen, though, and I definitely got the impression that they were hoping to have it out before the weird hardbacks like Infernals and Alchemicals.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That sounds good, I know a certain player who has wanted to have a glowing cuttlefish...or maybe jellyfish as an familiar for years. This sounds like the perfect setting for it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T17:38:30-07:00","id":165435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuddenThunder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/29335-who-can-grant-exigent-exaltations-who-can-be-granted-one?p=68970#post68970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well that depends a bit on what exactly the Exigence is, something very little has been said about.</div> </div> </div> </div>It occurs to me that what exactly the Exigence <i>is </i>might very well be left mysterious.<br /> <br /> So in some games, it could be fashioned from the still-living body of the last, tortured unicorn and fueled by the souls of orphans, and others it might made from ideals and be fueled by humanity's overflowing hopes. But it doesn't have to be EITHER of those things if it doesn't work for your games.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ochre</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/29335-who-can-grant-exigent-exaltations-who-can-be-granted-one?p=29765#post29765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah I'm a bit worried that, because Exigents were announced as a thing now, that people's creative efforts would focus all Exalt creation into Exigents <i>as a category</i>... Want to make up a new Exalt type? Nah, just make an Exigent. Have a cool idea that doesn't fall in the Terrestrial/Celestial category? Exigent. Exigent? Exigent.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was determined to make Fair Folk Exalts in the last edition (before I decided to wait for the new edition's core rules), and even in light of Exigence, I'm <i>still </i>gonna make them derive from Fair Folk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T17:42:16-07:00","id":165438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/29335-who-can-grant-exigent-exaltations-who-can-be-granted-one?p=69392#post69392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would design animal-totemed Exigents around familiars, rather than shapeshifting.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, Skitter and Bitch, from <i>Worm</i>?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T08:52:12-07:00","id":165969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/29335-who-can-grant-exigent-exaltations-who-can-be-granted-one?p=164709#post164709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if they were reclassified to a vaguely defined type of <b>non-human exalt</b>, as was at least partly implied by their original fluff?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's more or less what I want, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T09:08:17-07:00","id":165982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/29335-who-can-grant-exigent-exaltations-who-can-be-granted-one?p=164709#post164709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering 2nd and 3rd circle demons can already make <b>akuma</b>, seems pretty unnecessary to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. When Erembour makes an Akuma, that Akuma doesn't get an entire charmset based around Erembour's powers. In First Edition the Akuma got access to spirit charms. In 2nd edition the Akuma got access to the Ebon Dragon's charms. <br /> <br /> What I want to see is the ability to created Exalted with charmset's based around the themes of demons - an Erembour themed charmset, or a Sigereth themed charmset, or whatever. <br /> <br /> Maybe there will be a new class of Akuma in 3rd edition that can get a charmset based around their 2nd or 3rd circle patron? I would be quite stoked if that happened. And if it doesn't, well, I might end up including it in my games anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T09:15:23-07:00","id":165991,"title":"","content":"Demons can still power up someone and give them access to demon charms in 2E. It's called endowing them into a demon-blooded. <br /> <br /> Hell, Akumaization is basically that but with Yozis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T09:35:28-07:00","id":166014,"title":"","content":"Akuma, neither in 1st edition nor 2nd edition, accomplish what I'm talking about. Maybe in third edition there will be a way for demons (with appropriate limitations) to create Akuma who can construct charms like that. It could be neat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T09:40:40-07:00","id":166019,"title":"","content":"The Exigent hardback is going to need a sidebar that goes &quot;THE EXIGENCE IS FOR GODS ONLY. IF YOU WANT OTHER BEINGS TO MAKE THEIR OWN EXALTED, MAKE SHIT UP.&quot; isn't it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T09:41:08-07:00","id":166021,"title":"","content":"Yeah, since other spirits have Endownment too, I really don't see the point of this silly thing called Exigent. If you want to use Ahlat-theme power so bad, create a God-Blood character and use your Ahlat-theme Spirit charms ! Also being Akuma is pretty fun, mindless slave is totally PC material right there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T10:15:24-07:00","id":166076,"title":"","content":"Akuma -&gt; Green Sun Prince ; Endowed Godblood -&gt; Exigent. In both cases it's the same concept, just with more power, freedom and flexibility.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 06-11-2014, 01:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T10:30:19-07:00","id":166084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/29335-who-can-grant-exigent-exaltations-who-can-be-granted-one?p=165982#post165982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not really. When Erembour makes an Akuma, that Akuma doesn't get an entire charmset based around Erembour's powers. In First Edition the Akuma got access to spirit charms. In 2nd edition the Akuma got access to the Ebon Dragon's charms.<br /> <br /> What I want to see is the ability to created Exalted with charmset's based around the themes of demons - an Erembour themed charmset, or a Sigereth themed charmset, or whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ever heard of a module called Broken-Winged Crane? There's a lot of interesting stuff there, one of them being Yozi-aspected hearthstones, that curiously also include hearthstones of <b>2nd and 3rd circle demons</b> of those yozis, because they count as aspects of their Yozi.<br /> <br /> An Akuma with charms of a 2nd Circle or 3rd Circle is just another aplication of the same principle, no big unconceivable deal - specially considering <b>it already happens</b> in Infernals, as <b>everything</b> that comes from <b>Sun Nimbus Flare</b> basically screams &quot;Ligier&quot;. The books have already provided the precedents for a ST to toy with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T10:33:43-07:00","id":166089,"title":"","content":"Infernal Exalted aren't what I want. Infernal Exalted are not what I'm talking about. And Infernal Exalted are getting totally redesigned from the ground up in 3rd edition.<br /> <br /> Akuma also aren't what I want, aren't what I'm talking about, and will be getting totally redesigned from the ground up in 3rd edition.<br /> <br /> So, I dunno where you're going with this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 06-11-2014, 01:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T12:31:24-07:00","id":166164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Affliction</span></b><br /> <br /> During the the five days of Calibration, or following a particularly inauspicious series of circumstances, a desperate mortals throws his prayers across the sands of Cecelyne and into the alleys of the Demon City. The denizens of Malfeas pay heed to the mortal's desires and reach out with a fist of burning emerald flames to bestow upon him the power of the Desolate Exaltation. <br /> <br /> A demon of the second or third circle uses the power of the Affliction to sheer away a portion of their own power and bestow it upon the mortal, where it festers and grows. The mortal gains the power to fulfill his cursed desires, while the demon dreams of his Chosen's glories. <br /> <br /> Demons most often bestow this power upon mortals with whom they share a Defining Intimacy. </div> </div> </div>There's an equivalent of the Exigence that's thematically appropriate to demons. I came up with it in <i>five minutes</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T12:47:36-07:00","id":166172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Hanged Man</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find &quot;Because the Unconquered Sun Says No&quot; a deeply unsatisfactory answer to the question of Demonic Exigents, considering that 1/6th of his very own Solar Exaltations have been subverted by Demons, and a further 1/3rd by Ghosts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find the assumptions that we're still going to be seeing set quantities of any Exalt-type except the Sids and that warping existing Exaltations is equivalent to creating an order-made type to be of extremely low utility as mechanisms for understanding the Exigence or the altered Solars, even without getting into how the narratively-based reasons for the process not working for demons are because it's a thing that gods petition the Unconquered Sun for the use of and the denizens of Malfeas are collectively in Sol's ill graces.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T12:50:37-07:00","id":166173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/29335-who-can-grant-exigent-exaltations-who-can-be-granted-one?p=166164#post166164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's an equivalent of the Exigence that's thematically appropriate to demons. I came up with it in <i>five minutes</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. And mechanically, it's probably going to operate almost exactly like an Exigence - you'll be making up a charmset based around the demon's conceptual space. It'll be an Exigence with a different name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T13:00:25-07:00","id":166183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/29335-who-can-grant-exigent-exaltations-who-can-be-granted-one?p=166173#post166173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure. And mechanically, it's probably going to operate almost exactly like an Exigence - you'll be making up a charmset based around the demon's conceptual space. It'll be an Exigence with a different name.</div> </div> </div> </div>In this sense, most existing Exaltations with a divine patron are &quot;an Exigence with a different name.&quot;<br /> <br /> I submit that this broad a definition of the Exigence is completely useless for any practical discussion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T13:16:26-07:00","id":166193,"title":"","content":"I think one other thing we're neglecting to consider as far as demonic exigence goes is that demons, at least the type with the autonomy to be doing this sort of thing, are not independent entities in the way gods are, but rather small chunks of yozi. As such, their power is not, on a fundamental level, theirs to give up in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T06:13:57-07:00","id":166887,"title":"","content":"I think a major reason why Exigence is gods only is because for the last couple of editions gods have generally been portrayed as boring middle managers that the world would be much better off without. Meanwhile demons have never had a problem with being cool while the chosen of elementals have overlap issues with Dragon-Blooded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T06:32:23-07:00","id":166897,"title":"","content":"It seems logical to me that the Yozis themselves would be <i>capable</i> of warping an exigence to the point where it accepts demonic essence, but have absolutely no reason to actually do so<i>. </i>And would possibly even be grossly offended by any requests for them to do so.<br /> <br /> Related thought: Exigents in Autochthonia. Good idea? Terrible Idea?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 06-12-2014, 09:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T06:51:12-07:00","id":166903,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/29335-who-can-grant-exigent-exaltations-who-can-be-granted-one?p=166897#post166897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Related thought: Exigents in Autochthonia. Good idea? Terrible Idea?</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that the whole deal of the Adamant Caste is to be agents of the Divine Ministers, I'm going to cast my vote as nay. I can't think of a use that would particularly enrich the setting of Autochthonia. At best they are superfluous, at worst they disrupt the unique relationship that the Autochthonians have with the Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T07:46:32-07:00","id":166928,"title":"","content":"Because the Ebon Dragon created the Unconquered Sun and therefor knew how he thought/did things and used this to twist what Sun created? Even then it took Ebon around 15-20K years to come up with a method that Might work. No one in Malfeas (as far as I know) has had that kind of time to study, say the god of the harvest for Sleepy Village. Also from memory it was Auto who created it, and he was already pissed at his siblings for breaking all his cool stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2080-protector152","name":"Protector152","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T07:55:12-07:00","id":166932,"title":"","content":"The solars were corruptible by the Yozis. They could, as I said earlier, presumably do the same to exigencies but they can't use them themselves (only a solar exaltation can take that much power without breaking) and they're unwilling to give their subordinates exalted of their own because that kinda went badly for them the last time it happened. Plus Cecelyne and SWLiHN would probably throw a fit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T08:37:51-07:00","id":166948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Hanged Man</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unfortunately, I'm not having any success thinking of a superior alternate answer for why the Exigents are locked down but the Solars are corruptable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, yes, the old &quot;Solars are X, therefore all Exalted must be X.&quot; <br /> <br /> The Exigence has nothing to do with Solar Exaltation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T08:51:35-07:00","id":166957,"title":"","content":"My theory is that what's kept Exigence from being corrupted and re-purposed like the Solar Essences were is the simple fact that it's not indestructible, if you try twisting it into a new form you're more likely to just destroy it.<br /> <br /> Solar Exaltations aren't weak because they can be turned into Abyssal or Infernal Exaltations, they're scary because you can turn them inside out and they still work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T09:00:09-07:00","id":166971,"title":"","content":"Actually, thinking more on the hypothetical &quot;Chosen of Demons&quot; I think an Exigence knockoff might hurt Malfeas' denizens because it'll be simpler to have The Chosen of Octavian causing a ruckus than Octavian himself.<br /> <br /> It can be done well certainly, however there is a risk of him getting upstaged by his own creation who can freely roam Creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T09:19:06-07:00","id":166982,"title":"","content":"I'd say the Exigence is more governed by the dictates of the Unconquered Sun because it's a flame that he distributes to others that would ostensibly be incapable of producing Exalted by themselves; it's something of himself that he's sharing, he has latitude for denying it utterly.<br /> <br /> The Essence of the Solar Exalted is something that is part of him, but also a bit beyond him, because it partakes of his own unstoppable nature, himself set into motion by himself, unlimited by any will including his own. He can't deny it, but that's not supposed to matter, because there shouldn't be anything to deny.<br /> <br /> But that also means he can't stop what went wrong with them on the path that led to the Usurpation.<br /> <br /> The Yozis and Deathlords haven't corrupted the Solar Essence; the Solars did that. The Yozis and Deathlords are just giving it some new clothes to really express itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T09:24:00-07:00","id":166984,"title":"","content":"Since Infernal won't be using Yozi charms anymore, would it's be reasonable to assume that their charmset will have more demon realm flavor thus solving the &quot;No Exigent for Demon&quot; issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T09:25:06-07:00","id":166986,"title":"","content":"Another problem might be that demons aren't demons <i>of </i>anything in particular. They have roles they take but they're not tied to the concepts the same way. You could say that rather than just being a container for a god's power, an exigence (and maybe even a true Exaltation) instead uses that power to forge a connection between the exigent/exalt and the concept that the god represents itself. This would also be why elementals can't use them, because they <i>are</i> the element rather than representatives of the concept of the element.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T09:47:28-07:00","id":167001,"title":"","content":"Except that the exigence will only become indestructible when it's keyed to the specific god. The raw material that the demons would need to use isn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T09:56:41-07:00","id":167011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/29335-who-can-grant-exigent-exaltations-who-can-be-granted-one?p=166887#post166887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a major reason why Exigence is gods only is because for the last couple of editions gods have generally been portrayed as boring middle managers that the world would be much better off without. Meanwhile demons have never had a problem with being cool while the chosen of elementals have overlap issues with Dragon-Blooded.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say another part of it is that the concept of the Exigence is being firmly embedded in the actual social dynamics of the gods of the Celestial Order; how they relate to one another, how their hierarchies are organised, how their criminality and corruption play out.<br /> <br /> Whatever else demons are, they just aren't part of that culture, and I'd say their involvement would could of distract from that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T10:08:26-07:00","id":167024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Hanged Man</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">2.) If Gods with appropriate natures can make a &quot;blank&quot; Exigence indestructible, why can't Demons with appropriate natures (I.E. 100% of the actual Yozis) do the same?</div> </div> </div> </div>Exigence != Exaltation.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T10:24:58-07:00","id":167035,"title":"","content":"There is probably a difference between an exigence reinforced by godly power (which might not be compatible with a demonically altered container and destroy it itself) and true exaltations which had to be indestructible in order to withstand the full might of the incarnae power they were meant to hold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T10:39:10-07:00","id":167048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Hanged Man</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Good lord, what nitpicky bullshit. You know exactly what I mean, but you've decided to turn this into a fight over technicalities. I expected better of a moderator.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps you should simply learn to use words correctly, hmm?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T10:43:00-07:00","id":167069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/29335-who-can-grant-exigent-exaltations-who-can-be-granted-one?p=165982#post165982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not really. When Erembour makes an Akuma, that Akuma doesn't get an entire charmset based around Erembour's powers. In First Edition the Akuma got access to spirit charms. In 2nd edition the Akuma got access to the Ebon Dragon's charms.<br /> <br /> What I want to see is the ability to created Exalted with charmset's based around the themes of demons - an Erembour themed charmset, or a Sigereth themed charmset, or whatever.<br /> <br /> Maybe there will be a new class of Akuma in 3rd edition that can get a charmset based around their 2nd or 3rd circle patron? I would be quite stoked if that happened. And if it doesn't, well, I might end up including it in my games anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, we <b>already</b> get some cases of Yozi essence and 3rd or 2nd Circle essence getting mixed-up - the hearthstones of 2nd &amp; 3rd circle demons as expressions of Yozi essence and the Green Sun Nimbus Flare charms as an even more blatant (and relevant) case, as they are totally about Ligier as a charmset <b>and yet</b> we get them as a branch of Malfeas' charms.<br /> <br /> My point was that, based on those facts, this &quot;filtering/tweaking of Yozi essence&quot; phenomena they exemplify, the making of, for example, an &quot;Eremour Akuma&quot; or even &quot;Makarios Akuma&quot; instead of an Akuma of the Ebon Dragon, should be perfectly acceptable to 2e. And unless the akuma are <b>also </b>rewritten so no one gets Yozi charms or anything similar, it would still be a viable explanation/excuse for demon-themed akuma in 3e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T10:47:11-07:00","id":167071,"title":"","content":"IIRC that's exactly what's happening, so there you go. <br /> <br /> Also I'm not sure Ligier counts as an example of that because he might actually be the result of a charm himself for which all of those are prerequisites.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T10:55:34-07:00","id":167077,"title":"","content":"I also feel as though making demons capable of using the Exigence would kind of gobble up and inflate the entire Black Market Exaltation concept, since that's logically the only way they'd be able to get access to it, and since I think that, as conceived, for access to the Exigence to go astray is an uncommon and fearful aberration of a thing, rather than a necessarily massive part in its narrative.<br /> <br /> If it was open to demons, it would be hard to shake the sense of it being a much more common thing, if a lot of people want to give demons Exalted and the only way they can do so is the illicit method.<br /> <br /> No, I think it's better that other Infernal Exalted be their own thing, like the Getimian or Liminal Exalted will be, rather than intruding on the force by which the King of Heaven magnanimously provides for those gods of the Heavenly Order (and in which those gods who are in defiance of its strictures occasionally sneak through or intercept).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T10:58:34-07:00","id":167080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/29335-who-can-grant-exigent-exaltations-who-can-be-granted-one?p=166986#post166986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could say that rather than just being a container for a god's power, an exigence (and maybe even a true Exaltation) instead uses that power to forge a connection between the exigent/exalt and the concept that the god represents itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find that unlikely, considering this:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Gods make Exigents. Abstract concepts do not make Exigents.<br /> <br /> An Exigent of heroism or an Exigent of sorcery is unworkable.<br /> <br /> If you want a certain kind of Exigent, make up a spirit to fit your needs. Note that gods should be more interesting than &quot;the god of sorcery.&quot; Don't exclude the political, bureaucratic, and upward/downward mobility that makes the gods interesting. (See also: Ahlat.) </div> </div> </div>I also get an impression that that Volcano Exalt works in a manner that refers to the nature of the patron volcano god in a manner that makes for some very distinct powers, rather than just volcano powers. Something about Pressure...<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T11:13:35-07:00","id":167089,"title":"","content":"Could easily be both. Remember that was musings on the differences between gods and demons, which came down in this case to a connection to raw concepts that demons lacked. <br /> <br /> A volcano exalt gets volcano powers filtered through the god whose power he holds. He has the god, plus their connection to volcanoes, plus anything he brings to the table","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T11:35:52-07:00","id":167106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Hanged Man</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Good lord, what nitpicky bullshit. You know exactly what I mean, but you've decided to turn this into a fight over technicalities. I expected better of a moderator.</div> </div> </div> </div>#1 It's not a fucking technicality, I clearly remember John saying that Exigence was a component and not a blank exaltation when we're talking about someone potentially subverting the process that's a pretty important difference.<br /> #2 You're the one who turned this into a fight.<br /> #3 Get out the thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T15:57:10-07:00","id":167316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dragonmystic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/29335-who-can-grant-exigent-exaltations-who-can-be-granted-one?p=29356#post29356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who can be granted one: That's pretty easy, it's only creatures with human souls. The same mechanisms work for Exigence soul-pairing as it does for the other Celestial Exaltations. If you can't exalt as a Solar (or Lunar,) you can't Exalt as an Exigent. So no Tyrant Lizard Exalts, sorry. Who can grant is much more open. It just seems that you need a certain level of power (no Lesser Gods), access to the Exigence from one way or another, and not be specifically barred from it by the Unconquered Sun, like demons. Other than that, it looks pretty unclear, probably on purpose so it can vary from ST to ST.</div> </div> </div> </div> This would suck if this is truly the case. i have no interest in including exigents in my game, but the ability of various gods to elevate non-human creatures to exalted like status appeals to me a great deal. for example, i would love to introduce a creature that was the Lord of all Horses who could possibly be befriended by the PCs as an ally. far, far more interesting than yet more exaltations for humans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/779-nusoardgraphite","name":"NuSoardGraphite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar779_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T15:58:41-07:00","id":167317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GSD</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/29335-who-can-grant-exigent-exaltations-who-can-be-granted-one?p=29435#post29435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just because demons don't use Exigence doesn't mean there can't be new Demon Chosen! It just means they weren't made via the Sun's blessings. Why would demons want that anyway? If you want them to exist, say they exist! The Exigence is an in-setting excuse to add new varieties of exalts, but it is by no means the only way they can exist.</div> </div> </div> </div> Exactly. &quot;Do as thou wilt&quot; should be the whole of the law.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/779-nusoardgraphite","name":"NuSoardGraphite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar779_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T16:07:22-07:00","id":167321,"title":"","content":"Personally I wouldn't rule out a black market exigence that has, shall we say, had it's warranty voided somewhat. A god trying to weld one onto some poor creature with horrendous side effects sounds like a pretty good plot line for the PCs to deal with, if nothing else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T16:19:49-07:00","id":167327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/29335-who-can-grant-exigent-exaltations-who-can-be-granted-one?p=167071#post167071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IIRC that's exactly what's happening, so there you go.<br /> <br /> Also I'm not sure Ligier counts as an example of that because he might actually be the result of a charm himself for which all of those are prerequisites.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why, is he <b>not </b>a 3rd circle demon and a fetich? Does not <b>every Yozi</b> have a fetich and 10+ 3rd circle souls? Not to mention that &quot;3rd circle as personified yozi charm&quot; would actually be more of a point in the direction i was going.<br /> <br /> As an aside, what charm are you speaking of? Because the only one i can remember is [Yozi] Pantheon Unfurling and it would apply to all 3rd circles, not just the Fetiches and certainly not only Ligier....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T16:23:57-07:00","id":167329,"title":"","content":"Some of the later stuff implies that Malfeas had two fetiches at one point, Ligier being the second. He was basically a Primordial Time Lord. (Two hearts)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T17:53:55-07:00","id":167382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/29335-who-can-grant-exigent-exaltations-who-can-be-granted-one?p=167077#post167077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also feel as though making demons capable of using the Exigence would kind of gobble up and inflate the entire Black Market Exaltation concept, since that's logically the only way they'd be able to get access to it, and since I think that, as conceived, for access to the Exigence to go astray is an uncommon and fearful aberration of a thing, rather than a necessarily massive part in its narrative.<br /> <br /> If it was open to demons, it would be hard to shake the sense of it being a much more common thing, if a lot of people want to give demons Exalted and the only way they can do so is the illicit method.<br /> <br /> No, I think it's better that other Infernal Exalted be their own thing, like the Getimian or Liminal Exalted will be, rather than intruding on the force by which the King of Heaven magnanimously provides for those gods of the Heavenly Order (and in which those gods who are in defiance of its strictures occasionally sneak through or intercept).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I agree with that. Noting of course the *mechanically* we can make infernal exalted using the exigent rules...which SHOULD COME OUT APPROXIMATELY ONE PICOSECOND AFTER 3E CORE OR i WIWLL-ahem, pardon me. <br /> <br /> in any case, thematically, I don't think the Yozi's or demons should be able ot use the same method the gods use to make exigents-- becuse if they can it begs the question of A. why aren't there lots of 'em, (consider how many 3rd/p;owerful 2nd circle demons there are) and why it's not dominating the game. <br /> Additionally, let's face it, if a demon has to use a black market exaltation there are a LOT more stories yo can run from both ends....<br /> <br /> &quot;there's an exaltation just waiting for us to snag-- think what we could do against the realm with that kind of power...&quot;<br /> &quot;where is it?&quot;<br /> &quot;Wiating for a suitable candidate...&quot;<br /> &quot;WHERE?&quot;<br /> &quot;Ligers Forge.&quot;<br /> &quot;.... What the hell, I like to live dangerously. I'm in.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T20:03:06-07:00","id":167445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/29335-who-can-grant-exigent-exaltations-who-can-be-granted-one?p=167329#post167329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some of the later stuff implies that Malfeas had two fetiches at one point, Ligier being the second. He was basically a Primordial Time Lord. (Two hearts)</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, the thing about Rumelia and how Malfeas supposedly had two fetiches at some time in the past. Considering it came up in stuff from the Ink Monkeys, the tale can be canon or not according to preference - and the tale being canon in one's game does not have to mean it is a <b>true</b> tale...<br /> <br /> But more importantly, that on itself does not make my Yozi-3rd circle correlation invalid - the Yozi soul hierarchies are full of individual peculiarities, like Adorjan having 20+ souls, Orabilis having Essence 10 (what might justify calling him Cecelyne's 2nd Fetich) and who knows what other stuff.<br /> <br /> Fluff or mechanics that <b>contradicted/denied</b> the idea of a 2nd or 3rd circle demon's power being a filtered/specialized reflection of the Yozi's own, <b>that </b>would be problematic to my take on the possibility of &quot;tunning&quot; akuma to certain demons. Nothing about Ligier that has been said at present, afaik, comes even close to doing that.<br /> <br /> On the matter of Exigence being a gods-only thing, honestly it is as big or as little a deal as Investiture of Infernal Glory being a demons-only thing.<br /> Each group with its tricks - and elementals get the short stick again. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T20:54:15-07:00","id":167517,"title":"","content":"On Demons, I would imagine the Law of Diminishment would be more difficult to get past when it also 'Grandfathers' in god-beings that can directly control you. Even if, say, Orabilis REALLY needs an Exalt to help Lucien stop another Usurpation or w/e. Unless Cecelyne is on board with taking a reduction in power she can just Nope that idea right out of town. Considering that she is the embodiment of selfish entitlement, it seems unlikely.<br /> <br /> This isn't to say that it wouldn't happen, just a story element that seems interesting.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, TED would be all ABOUT hobbling his own power for questionable gain. It's basically his entire wheelhouse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T23:03:14-07:00","id":167600,"title":"","content":"Demons can already make Akuma. thematically it's completely unnecessary for demons to be able to create exigents because they already have a method for empowering their followers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/779-nusoardgraphite","name":"NuSoardGraphite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar779_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-13T03:30:20-07:00","id":167714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NuSoardGraphite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/29335-who-can-grant-exigent-exaltations-who-can-be-granted-one?p=167600#post167600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demons can already make Akuma. thematically it's completely unnecessary for demons to be able to create exigents because they already have a method for empowering their followers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Especially since 3E akuma are not sockpuppets for the Yozi's but based on much more faustian bargains.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-13T06:23:16-07:00","id":167824,"title":"","content":"I'd say it's highly unsatisfying to make any flavour of akuma the only recourse for other Infernal Exalted, between the idea that you've only got an already existing Exalt with some extra bells tacked on, and the sense that they can only ever be cribbing off of the limited existing pool. Whether they're sock puppets or not, I find something offputting about the idea that when akuma are a <i>thing</i>, as opposed to just being an example of that kind of Exalt with some toes in a few Infernal pacts... it feels like the worst of both worlds; all you get is a vague hodge podge. Especially if the pool of Exalts is being expanded anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-13T09:32:09-07:00","id":167979,"title":"","content":"I'm prepared to wait and see. The developers know that the term &quot;Akuma&quot; has a lot of baggage to it even if they change what it means.<br /> <br /> It'd be interesting if individual demons had their own title for people they've made a pact with, for example someone who makes a Pact with Mara could be called her Paramour while Ligier might call someone he had a contract with his Apprentice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-13T09:40:49-07:00","id":168003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/29335-who-can-grant-exigent-exaltations-who-can-be-granted-one?p=167824#post167824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say it's highly unsatisfying to make any flavour of akuma the only recourse for other Infernal Exalted, between the idea that you've only got an already existing Exalt with some extra bells tacked on, and the sense that they can only ever be cribbing off of the limited existing pool. Whether they're sock puppets or not, I find something offputting about the idea that when akuma are a <i>thing</i>, as opposed to just being an example of that kind of Exalt with some toes in a few Infernal pacts... it feels like the worst of both worlds; all you get is a vague hodge podge. Especially if the pool of Exalts is being expanded anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well you see, i like the current idea of an extremely limited pool of exalted essences floating around out there. They are rare and very special under those circumstances. make them more common and they become less so. this is my main problem with introducing more exalted types (exigents, liminals getimians etc). i also believe that the introduction of exigents will likely make the default solars, lunars and terrestrials much less attractive if you have the ability of creating your own exalted theme and powers. while in general i love the idea of players being in complete control of how they create their character, superpowers and all, i am so enamored with the dynamic in exalted 1 and 2 that i dont want it messed with at all. As it stands now, based on what i've heard about some of the campaign changes, i might just be utilizing 3rd edition game mechanics with 1st and 2cnd edition campaign materials.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/779-nusoardgraphite","name":"NuSoardGraphite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar779_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-13T09:59:16-07:00","id":168030,"title":"","content":"The total number of all the old + new Exalted combined is still a lot lower than the number of Dragon-Blooded in the Realm.<br /> <br /> Edit: also<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NuSoardGraphite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/29335-who-can-grant-exigent-exaltations-who-can-be-granted-one?p=168003#post168003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> i also believe that the introduction of exigents will likely make the default solars, lunars and terrestrials much less attractive if you have the ability of creating your own exalted theme and powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>an Exigent is probably going to be weaker than a Solar, a while back people were saying stuff like &quot;why would ever I play a Twilight again when I can be a Chosen of Invention?&quot;<br /> Holden's answer was simple, the Chosen of Invention doesn't get to out-invent the Twilight it's just that their charmset would be based on using innovation to solve problems. The Twilight can get bored of inventing things and become a master swordsman because that's how Solars roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 06-13-2014, 01:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-13T15:08:06-07:00","id":168292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NuSoardGraphite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/29335-who-can-grant-exigent-exaltations-who-can-be-granted-one?p=168003#post168003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well you see, i like the current idea of an extremely limited pool of exalted essences floating around out there. They are rare and very special under those circumstances. make them more common and they become less so.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't find this statement very coherent with the idea that Hell doesn't require anything kind of equivalent to Exigence because they already have Akuma.<br /> <br /> If one is already conceding the possibility of Exigents or other Exalts, then Akuma are unsatisfying. If one is sticking to the idea of only the currently known Exalted... then Akuma are still unsatisfying, since they try to act as a separate kind of thing even though they can only exist by skimming off of the other things.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T13:28:48-07:00","id":169202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/29335-who-can-grant-exigent-exaltations-who-can-be-granted-one?p=168030#post168030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">an Exigent is probably going to be weaker than a Solar, a while back people were saying stuff like &quot;why would ever I play a Twilight again when I can be a Chosen of Invention?&quot;<br /> Holden's answer was simple, the Chosen of Invention doesn't get to out-invent the Twilight it's just that their charmset would be based on using innovation to solve problems. The Twilight can get bored of inventing things and become a master swordsman because that's how Solars roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Chosen of Invention would be an unusually narrow kind of concept. Obviously it depends on the concept, yet I can imagine a Exigent of Blades could be as great as Solars at every ability, just that his charms would be stretching lots of combat metaphors to do it, expressed through all the different abilities. That would give him a style, but edged combat influenced Charms can be broad and not necessarily leave him weaker than a Solar, who also faces constraints on his style of his own sort.<br /> <br /> And, mind, when you're being an Exigent, you're Exigent of a god, not a narrow concept. So Janest does get lots of wheat-y and harvest-y powers, but also the general nature of Ten Sheaves. <br /> <br /> If you have say, a really thematically broad god as your patron, like Ahlat, and for some reason manage to pull a &quot;The Exigent is of a Solar level power&quot; justifiably in your game, somehow, then there's a lot you can do.<br /> <br /> I still wouldn't worry too much about the stuff NuSoardGraphite worries about - the Solars and other Celestials will still comfortably have plenty of appeal based on who they are, even without their power, based on their style, being part of a larger splat, how box ready they are to go and how they fit into the grand story of the world. The Exigents can kind of enhance the stories of these splats, because if someone wants to play or introduce a character who would be path breaking for any of the splats, they can do so without altering the existing splats.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T19:07:15-07:00","id":173481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/29335-who-can-grant-exigent-exaltations-who-can-be-granted-one?p=167979#post167979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm prepared to wait and see. The developers know that the term &quot;Akuma&quot; has a lot of baggage to it even if they change what it means.</div> </div> </div> </div>See also: Chimera. Which evokes very strong images thanks to Second Edition, and which will be completely different in Third.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T19:54:52-07:00","id":173537,"title":"","content":"I absolutely <b>loved </b>the idea of Exigents, but I can say that it would take a miracle or two for them to become my number one favorite instead of Solars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T09:09:32-07:00","id":174181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/29335-who-can-grant-exigent-exaltations-who-can-be-granted-one?p=173481#post173481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See also: Chimera. Which evokes very strong images thanks to Second Edition, and which will be completely different in Third.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but people who've never played Exalted before are familiar with the word &quot;chimera&quot; being used to describe a fusion of two or more animals. Calling someone who makes Faustian pacts for power an Akuma is much less natural and only really likely to stay for the sake of a Kindred of the East connection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T09:23:40-07:00","id":174190,"title":"","content":"What's happening to chimera?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T09:29:08-07:00","id":174193,"title":"","content":"It seems a 3rd edition Chimera will be a Lunar with two (or more) spirit shapes and a warform that's reflective of this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T09:30:46-07:00","id":174212,"title":"","content":"That... sounds really boring honestly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T09:43:51-07:00","id":174223,"title":"","content":"It's all in the execution.<br /> 2nd edition style Chimera were unplayable and 90% of their role could easily be replaced with monsters that the wyld spat out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T09:51:20-07:00","id":174235,"title":"","content":"Probably just as well; I don't think Lunars were well served by giving them this specialized sub-category that had to go off in its own little world with its own special rules that were only tangentially related to Lunars at best, and tried to act as though it was this fearsome existential dilemma even though default characters were immune to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T09:55:50-07:00","id":174241,"title":"","content":"I wonder... Exigents might be variable enough to be basically anything, at least because the mechanics for making one provide for making basically any Exalted, but I wonder if there might be a little bit of a connective theme of them being a kind of folk hero focused on unconventional aesthetic, related to but distinct from the more conventional kinds of folk heroes that the Celestial Exalted are, and the more odd kinds of other Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T10:08:01-07:00","id":174254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/29335-who-can-grant-exigent-exaltations-who-can-be-granted-one?p=174235#post174235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably just as well; I don't think Lunars were well served by giving them this specialized sub-category that had to go off in its own little world with its own special rules that were only tangentially related to Lunars at best, and tried to act as though it was this fearsome existential dilemma even though default characters were immune to it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, but at least chimeras were a <i>thing</i>. This doesn't seem enough to even warrant a label. Like, wow, you can turn into a bull <i>and </i>a hawk? And you didn't need to kill either? Dude that is off the wall!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T10:11:40-07:00","id":174257,"title":"","content":"We've also been told that 3rd edition spirit shape is going to do more than be the animal you turn into by default.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T10:16:51-07:00","id":174261,"title":"","content":"Alright, that might salvage it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T11:01:24-07:00","id":174285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/29335-who-can-grant-exigent-exaltations-who-can-be-granted-one?p=174254#post174254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like, wow, you can turn into a bull <i>and </i>a hawk? And you didn't need to kill either? Dude that is off the wall!</div> </div> </div> </div>By &quot;two or more spirit shapes&quot;, think hybridized forms, not separate ones.<br /> <br /> There's also something in it being kind of stuck between an attempted transition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T14:32:19-07:00","id":174565,"title":"","content":"I know that I'm tempted to, once the lunar book is out, make a Lunar as a fire-breathing, snake-tailed, two-headed lion/goat nightmare.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://postimage.org/\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"http://s10.postimg.org/iiyv7d5qx/chimera.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":868,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","user":"danelsan","date":". 06-19-2014, 10:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T14:54:32-07:00","id":174586,"title":"","content":"You could totally have that in 2E. Admittedly you'd need essence 6 but it's doable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T14:58:21-07:00","id":174587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/29335-who-can-grant-exigent-exaltations-who-can-be-granted-one?p=174565#post174565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know that I'm tempted to, once the lunar book is out, make a Lunar as a fire-breathing, snake-tailed, two-headed lion/goat nightmare.</div> </div> </div> </div>I want a chicken-yeddim.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T15:15:46-07:00","id":174614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/29335-who-can-grant-exigent-exaltations-who-can-be-granted-one?p=174565#post174565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know that I'm tempted to, once the lunar book is out, make a Lunar as a fire-breathing, snake-tailed, two-headed lion/goat nightmare.</div> </div> </div> </div>Coolness. With the Night's Master thread floating back up... Perhaps a wolf-headed, serpent-tailed boar Lunar, wronged by a petty act of cruelty and thus driven to pursue revenge and the darkest depths of Sorcery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":". 06-19-2014, 06:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}